# The ruling "Deadly Cover-Up allows its controller to exile a basic land", and "any number of cards": Bot2's cleanup discard
# leaves an Island in its graveyard, Bot1 exiles it, then takes only two of Bot2's seven Islands in hand and three Islands from
# its library, leaving the rest. Bot2 shuffles and draws two cards, one for each card exiled from its hand (not for the three
# from the library or the one from the graveyard). Exile: Griselbrand (the evidence) and six Islands.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Ruby
Faithless Looting
Black Lotus
Deadly Cover-Up
Griselbrand
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
